  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Emergent obligated $370M in FY2026 to date. Emergent won 177 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.1M and obligations up 2.0% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations have varied since FY21, peaking at $520M in FY23 and then falling to $363M in FY25 before rising to $370M in FY26. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $102M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $70.6M and the Department of State with $49.3M. Other Computer Related Services is Emergent's largest market, with $333M in obligations, and Electronic Computer Manufacturing is the second market at $34.3M. Several smaller NAICS markets account for the remaining obligations, including Software Publishers and various computing infrastructure and wholesaler categories. These figures are contract obligations except where noted otherwise for award-value tables. This snapshot shows where federal demand sits for Emergent so far in FY2026 and which agencies and markets drive most of the current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What are Emergent's recent obligation trends?",
        "body": "Emergent obligated $370M in FY2026 to date. Obligations moved from $470M in FY21 to $518M in FY22, $520M in FY23, $396M in FY24, $363M in FY25, and $370M in FY26. Obligations are up 2.0% year over year between FY25 and FY26. The average award size for FY2026 to date is $2.1M across 177 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Emergent's largest federal buyers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $102M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $70.6M, and the Department of State obligated $49.3M in FY2026 to date. Other notable buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $47.8M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $28.9M. Other Computer Related Services is the largest market at $333M, followed by Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $34.3M. Several smaller markets account for the remainder, including Software Publishers and computing infrastructure categories."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Emergent make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Emergent obligated $370M in FY2026 to date. Emergent won 177 awards so far this fiscal year, the average award size is $2.1M, and obligations are up 2.0% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $470M in FY21, $518M in FY22, $520M in FY23, $396M in FY24, and $363M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Emergent?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense obligated $102M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $70.6M, and the Department of State obligated $49.3M. Other federal buyers in FY2026 to date include the Department of Homeland Security at $47.8M, the Department of Health and Human Services at $28.9M, and the Department of the Treasury at $24.9M, among others."
    },
